@prefix : <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/tagging.owl#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix xml: <http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix tagging: <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/tagging.owl#> .
@prefix tagging2: <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/tagging.owl#> .
@prefix agentrole: <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/agentrole.owl#> .
@prefix situation: <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/situation.owl#> .
@prefix timeinterval: <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/timeinterval.owl#> .
@prefix classification: <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/classification.owl#> .
@prefix collectionentity: <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/collectionentity.owl#> .
@prefix cpannotationschema: <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#> .
@prefix intensionextension: <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/intensionextension.owl#> .
@prefix timeindexedsituation: <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/timeindexedsituation.owl#> .
@base <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/tagging.owl> .

<http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/tagging.owl> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                                            owl:imports <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/agentrole.owl> ,
                                                                        <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/collectionentity.owl> ,
                                                                        <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/intensionextension.owl> ,
                                                                        <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/timeindexedsituation.owl> ;
                                                            dcterms:description "To represent a tagging situation, in which someone uses a term, from a list of a folksonomy, to tag something (or the content of something). We might also want to represent the time and the polarity of the tagging."^^xsd:string ;
                                                            dcterms:title "Tagging Pattern"^^xsd:string ;
                                                            cpannotationschema:coversRequirements "Who is tagging (the content of) what, by using what term from what folksonomy?, Which polarity has the tagging?" ;
                                                            cpannotationschema:hasAuthor "Aldo Gangemi" ;
                                                            cpannotationschema:hasComponent "AgentRole" ,
                                                                                            "CollectionEntity" ,
                                                                                            "IntensionExtension" ;
                                                            cpannotationschema:hasConsequences """We are able to represent data about tagging activities from web 2.0 applications, from document annotation projects, or from RDFa documents.
""" ;
                                                            cpannotationschema:hasIntent "To represent a tagging situation, in which someone uses a term, from a list of a folksonomy, to tag something (or the content of something). We might also want to represent the time and the polarity of the tagging."^^xsd:string ;
                                                            cpannotationschema:hasUnitTest """SELECT ?a ?tag ?time ?thing ?folk ?pol
WHERE { 
?x :byAgent ?a .
?x :usingTag ?tag .
?x atTime ?time .
?x :forEntity ?thing .
?x :fromCloud ?folk .
?x :hasPolarity ?pol }""" ;
                                                            cpannotationschema:isSpecializationOf "TimeIndexedSituation" ;
                                                            cpannotationschema:relatedCPs "Topic" ;
                                                            cpannotationschema:scenarios """A Flickr picture showing a leopard, tagged with the Tag 'leopard',A Flickr picture showing a boy surfing with a sombrero hat, tagged with the Tag 'cool', A Flickr picture tagged as 'taken in Sicily'
""" ;
                                                            rdfs:comment """Curated by OntoBoard 1.155.0, so that the pattern passes ODK's quality report with its default profile, names every term with a label, and is consistent and coherent. Changes: label moved to skos:prefLabel x1; label moved to skos:altLabel x1; label added x29; term declared x4;
- header: dcterms:title \"Tagging Pattern\" - the library's name for the pattern
- header: dcterms:description - the library's description of the pattern
Each change is listed under \"curated\" in the pattern's metadata.json in OntoBoard's pattern library."""@en ,
                                                                         """The tagging ontology drafted by Tom Gruber in FOL, and formalized here in OWL by Aldo Gangemi with pattern-based design.
A Tag is here classified as a linguistic object that is used in the context of a Tagging Situation, which also involves a (tagged) Entity, an Agent, and a Folksonomy."""^^xsd:string ;
                                                            rdfs:label "Tagging ontology" ;
                                                            owl:versionInfo "1.1 added rdfs:isDefinedBy for all named entities"^^xsd:string ,
                                                                            """1.2
- Added annotations for ODP publication
1.1
- Revised some axioms involving restrictions on the Tagging situation class
1.0
- Created by Aldo Gangemi, March 2007""" .

#################################################################
#    Annotation properties
#################################################################

###  http://purl.org/dc/terms/description
dcterms:description rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                    rdfs:label "Description (DC terms)"@en .


###  http://purl.org/dc/terms/title
dcterms:title rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
              rdfs:label "Title"@en .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#coversRequirements
cpannotationschema:coversRequirements rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                      rdfs:label "covers requirements"@en .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#hasAuthor
cpannotationschema:hasAuthor rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                             rdfs:label "has author"@en .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#hasComponent
cpannotationschema:hasComponent rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                rdfs:label "has component"@en .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#hasConsequences
cpannotationschema:hasConsequences rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                   rdfs:label "has consequences"@en .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#hasIntent
cpannotationschema:hasIntent rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                             rdfs:label "has intent"@en .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#hasUnitTest
cpannotationschema:hasUnitTest rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                               rdfs:label "has unit test"@en .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#isSpecializationOf
cpannotationschema:isSpecializationOf rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                      rdfs:label "is specialization of"@en .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#relatedCPs
cpannotationschema:relatedCPs rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                              rdfs:label "related c ps"@en .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#scenarios
cpannotationschema:scenarios rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                             rdfs:label "scenarios"@en .


###  http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment
rdfs:comment rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy
rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label
rdfs:label rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo
owl:versionInfo rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel
skos:altLabel rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
              rdfs:label "alternative label"@en .


###  http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel
skos:prefLabel rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
               rdfs:label "preferred label"@en .


#################################################################
#    Object Properties
#################################################################

###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/collectionentity.owl#hasMember
collectionentity:hasMember rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                           rdfs:label "has member"@en .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/collectionentity.owl#isMemberOf
collectionentity:isMemberOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                            rdfs:label "is member of"@en .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/situation.owl#hasSetting
situation:hasSetting rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                     rdfs:label "hasSetting"^^xsd:string .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/situation.owl#isSettingFor
situation:isSettingFor rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                       rdfs:label "isSettingFor"^^xsd:string .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/tagging.owl#byAgent
tagging2:byAgent rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf situation:isSettingFor ;
                 owl:inverseOf tagging2:isTaggingAgentIn ;
                 rdfs:domain tagging:Tagging ;
                 rdfs:range agentrole:Agent ;
                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/tagging.owl> ;
                 rdfs:label "by agent"@en .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/tagging.owl#isTagUsedIn
tagging2:isTagUsedIn rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                     rdfs:subPropertyOf situation:hasSetting ;
                     owl:inverseOf tagging2:usingTag ;
                     rdfs:domain tagging:Tag ;
                     rdfs:range tagging:Tagging ;
                     rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/tagging.owl> ;
                     rdfs:label "isTagUsedIn" .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/tagging.owl#isTaggingAgentIn
tagging2:isTaggingAgentIn rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                          rdfs:subPropertyOf situation:hasSetting ;
                          rdfs:domain agentrole:Agent ;
                          rdfs:range tagging:Tagging ;
                          rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/tagging.owl> ;
                          rdfs:label "is tagging agent in"@en .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/tagging.owl#usingTag
tagging2:usingTag rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                  rdfs:subPropertyOf situation:isSettingFor ;
                  rdfs:domain tagging:Tagging ;
                  rdfs:range tagging:Tag ;
                  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/tagging.owl> ;
                  rdfs:label "usingTag" .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/timeindexedsituation.owl#atTime
timeindexedsituation:atTime rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                            rdfs:label "at time"@en .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/timeindexedsituation.owl#forEntity
timeindexedsituation:forEntity rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                               rdfs:label "for entity"@en .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/timeindexedsituation.owl#hasTimeIndexedSetting
timeindexedsituation:hasTimeIndexedSetting rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                           rdfs:label "has time indexed setting"@en .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/tagging.owl#fromCloud
tagging:fromCloud rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                  rdfs:subPropertyOf situation:isSettingFor ;
                  owl:inverseOf tagging:isTagCloudOf ;
                  rdfs:domain tagging:Tagging ;
                  rdfs:range tagging:Folksonomy ;
                  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/tagging.owl> ;
                  rdfs:label "from cloud" .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/tagging.owl#isTagCloudOf
tagging:isTagCloudOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                     rdfs:subPropertyOf situation:hasSetting ;
                     rdfs:domain tagging:Folksonomy ;
                     rdfs:range tagging:Tagging ;
                     rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/tagging.owl> ;
                     rdfs:label "is tag cloud of" .


#################################################################
#    Data properties
#################################################################

###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/tagging.owl#hasPolarity
tagging:hasPolarity rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                    rdfs:domain tagging:Tagging ;
                    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
                    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/tagging.owl> ;
                    rdfs:label "has polarity"@en .


#################################################################
#    Classes
#################################################################

###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/agentrole.owl#Agent
agentrole:Agent rdf:type owl:Class ;
                rdfs:label "Agent"@en .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/classification.owl#Concept
classification:Concept rdf:type owl:Class ;
                       rdfs:subClassOf intensionextension:SocialObject ;
                       rdfs:label "Concept"^^xsd:string .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/collectionentity.owl#Collection
collectionentity:Collection rdf:type owl:Class ;
                            rdfs:label "Collection"@en .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/intensionextension.owl#InformationObject
intensionextension:InformationObject rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                     rdfs:label "Information object"@en .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/intensionextension.owl#SocialObject
intensionextension:SocialObject rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                rdfs:label "Social object"@en .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/timeindexedsituation.owl#TimeIndexedSituation
timeindexedsituation:TimeIndexedSituation rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                          rdfs:label "Time indexed situation"@en .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/timeinterval.owl#TimeInterval
timeinterval:TimeInterval rdf:type owl:Class ;
                          rdfs:label "Time interval"@en .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/tagging.owl#Folksonomy
tagging:Folksonomy rdf:type owl:Class ;
                   rdfs:subClassOf collectionentity:Collection ,
                                   intensionextension:InformationObject ,
                                   [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                     owl:onProperty collectionentity:hasMember ;
                                     owl:someValuesFrom tagging:Tag
                                   ] ;
                   rdfs:comment "A collection of tags or metadata that have no formal semantics, and are typically used sparsely to annotate texts, images, bookmarks, etc. Folksonomies are typically maintained by communities through web-based services or systems, and do not have any systematic intent, such as that shared by KOS(es)."^^xsd:string ;
                   rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/tagging.owl> ;
                   rdfs:label "Folksonomy"@en ;
                   skos:altLabel "Tag cloud"^^xsd:string .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/tagging.owl#Tag
tagging:Tag rdf:type owl:Class ;
            rdfs:subClassOf intensionextension:InformationObject ,
                            [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                              owl:onProperty collectionentity:isMemberOf ;
                              owl:someValuesFrom tagging:Folksonomy
                            ] ,
                            [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                              owl:onProperty timeindexedsituation:hasTimeIndexedSetting ;
                              owl:someValuesFrom tagging:Tagging
                            ] ;
            rdfs:comment """The typical elements of folksonomies, used to add a hint for the interpretation of web resources in so-called situations of 'Tagging'.
Tags are considered here as InformationObject(s) that have a folksonomy as their schema.
A Tag is typically used to add an element of interpretation to some document, i.e. 'forcing' the reader to see that document from the viewpoint that can be built by pairing the Tag interpretation with the document interpretation. For example, an image of St. Peter's dome can be tagged as 'Michelangelo', 'Big ovoid', 'trip to Rome', etc., thus forcing the interpretation of the dome image towards artistic design, geometry, or private memories.""" ;
            rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/tagging.owl> ;
            rdfs:label "Tag"@en ;
            skos:prefLabel "Tag"@it .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/tagging.owl#Tagging
tagging:Tagging rdf:type owl:Class ;
                rdfs:subClassOf timeindexedsituation:TimeIndexedSituation ,
                                [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                  owl:onProperty tagging2:byAgent ;
                                  owl:someValuesFrom agentrole:Agent
                                ] ,
                                [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                  owl:onProperty tagging2:usingTag ;
                                  owl:someValuesFrom tagging:Tag
                                ] ,
                                [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                  owl:onProperty timeindexedsituation:atTime ;
                                  owl:someValuesFrom timeinterval:TimeInterval
                                ] ,
                                [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                  owl:onProperty timeindexedsituation:forEntity ;
                                  owl:someValuesFrom owl:Thing
                                ] ,
                                [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                  owl:onProperty tagging:fromCloud ;
                                  owl:someValuesFrom tagging:Folksonomy
                                ] ,
                                [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                  owl:onProperty tagging:hasPolarity ;
                                  owl:cardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                ] ;
                rdfs:comment """The tagging relation, represented as a class following the situation design pattern.
It includes, as suggested by Gruber's proposal, a Tag, a (tagged) Thing, a (source) Folksonomy, a (tagger) Agent, and a polarity. Moreover, this axiomatization also includes a TimeInterval at which the tagging happens. The tagged thing can actually have a content that is the actual target of tagging.

For example, let's see the semantics of the following cases of Tagging:
(1) a Flickr picture showing a leopard, tagged with the Tag 'leopard'
(2) a Flickr picture showing Tim Berners-Lee, tagged with the Tag 'Tim'
(3) a Flickr picture showing Tim Berners-Lee, tagged with the Tag 'the founder of the semantic web'
(4) a Flickr picture showing a girl having breakfast, tagged with the Tag 'me'
(5) a Flickr picture showing a boy surfing with a sombrero hat, tagged with the Tag 'cool'
(6) a Flickr picture that is tagged as 'taken in Sicily'
In cases (1)-(5), the pictures are about certain entities (a certain leopard, Tim Berners-Lee, a certain girl, a surfing boy), and the tag addresses tham, rather than the pictures (case 6).

Therefore, an act of tagging is not different from a generic linguistic act, except that it necessarily references something that is also referenced by a web resource: a condition that of course does not apply to generalized linguistic acts.""" ;
                rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/tagging.owl> ;
                rdfs:label "Tagging"@en .


###  http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing
owl:Thing rdf:type owl:Class .


